 verifier-efficiency" as TAUTOLOGY (oracle-fed verifier)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

An adversarial verifier-audit (workflow wf_5c1967c2-7f9) found, and a direct code
read confirmed, that the exp3929 action_efficiency_ratio=1.959 is circular:

  encode_rich_candidate_action() (python/carnot/agentic/arc_agi3_action_efficiency.py:411)
  -> task_potential() reads ORACLE goal fields (key/switch/gate/goal) the synthetic
     env exposes by construction to compute potential_delta, then PLANTS a hard-coded
     string: progress -> "1 + 0 = 1. The answer is 1."; non-progress ->
     "1 + 0 = 2. The answer is 0. actually inconsistent."
  -> the energy verifier then "detects" the contradiction it was handed.

`if 'inconsistent' in step_text` reproduces the identical 1.96x. The encoder, not
the energy function, makes every decision; the verifier scores a planted label, not
the grid. This is the TAUTOLOGY / GATE_PASSED_WITHOUT_DATA pattern.

Notable: scripts/adversarial_verify.py rates the artifact CLEAN — it catches numeric
tautologies, not this code-logic circularity (the JSON numbers are individually
plausible). Linter blind spot recorded for a future extension.

Action: stamped flagged_adversarial=true + corrigendum_2026_06_08 so the fabrication
gate quarantines it from any capstone/headline/"verifier=efficiency" aggregation.
The 1.96x must NOT be cited as evidence the Carnot verifier prunes real ARC actions;
a real M3 must derive the prune signal FROM the grid vs the INDUCED world-model (no
oracle) on the real games solved in M2. Data preserved (not retired).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
